{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b32a9976-0e68-4179-85b4-24af33ceaeb4","agentId":"a6f22e38681eea6df","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are the THEORY agent for a new FRA research direction. Produce a rigorous theory + a concrete, buildable synthetic-model spec. Work in /Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj.\n\n## READ FIRST (Read tool):\n- experiments/fra_win/THEORY.md — the converged FRA theory (the cell decomposition S[q,k]=Σ_{μν} u^μ_q u^ν_k ω_{μν}; cell = multiplicative AND; cell-level weight edit; magnitude law A≈reuse(marginal)/reuse(conjunction); the 5-clause win-checklist; score-space-vs-residual-space).\n- experiments/fra_win/RESULTS_SUMMARY.md — the 3 confirmed claims.\n- experiments/fra_hierarchy/CAMPAIGN.md — this campaign's hypothesis and risk.\n\n## THE DIRECTION (two coupled ideas):\n**(A) BROAD × BROAD cell-cutting — going UP the feature hierarchy.** Every confirmed FRA win is the LOWEST rung: a specific feature bound to a single token, so cutting a (query-feature × key-feature) cell just cuts a BIGRAM statistic. The PI's hypothesis: the interesting consequences come from BROAD features (each fires on MANY words) and HIGH in the hierarchy (abstract concepts). FLAGSHIP: cut the cell between a MISALIGNED-PERSONA feature (broad/abstract) and a DOMAIN feature → SELECTIVELY prevent emergent misalignment (EM) from generalizing to that domain, while preserving the persona's behavior in OTHER domains and the domain's normal (aligned) processing — something a linear persona-DIRECTION removal (DoM/SVD, which already works but is ALL-OR-NOTHING) cannot do.\n\n**(B) The REGRESSION protocol — FITTING which cells to cut.** Currently cells are chosen by top-magnitude (a heuristic that only works for single-token specifics) or hand-crafted differential cells. Generalize it: given a TARGET (a behavior/logit delta, an attention-pattern change, or a held-out collateral budget), SOLVE for the cell-coefficient mask — e.g. a sparse/L1-regularized regression of the behavior change onto per-cell ablations, \"the smallest cell-set that removes the behavior under a collateral cap.\" This subsumes top-K and differential cells, and is the natural way to FIND the broad cells that carry a concept→concept link.\n\n## THE KEY TENSION (must be central): FRA only cuts ATTENTION-routed links. A broad concept that generalizes via OV/MLP/a residual DIRECTION (our prior em_svd result: EM is removable as a weight-diff direction) is invisible to FRA. So: (1) CAN a broad×broad ATTENTION cell be cut selectively, in principle? [synthetic, the priority]; (2) WHICH real concept→concept links are attention-routed? [later, real-LLM].\n\n## RELEVANT THEORY HOOKS:\n- SynthSAEBench (arxiv 2602.14687): generates synthetic ground-truth features with controlled CORRELATION, HIERARCHY, and SUPERPOSITION. A broad/high feature can be modeled as an OR / parent of many narrow/child features.\n- Toy Models of Superposition (Elhage et al 2022): sparse features in superposition (d_model < #features), non-orthogonal directions → interference.\n- The SUPERPOSITION angle (likely the deep \"why\"): a broad feature in superposition overlaps many narrow features; a LINEAR steer that removes the broad direction incurs INTERFERENCE collateral (residual-space edit, proportional to feature overlap); a SCORE-SPACE cell-edit (FRA) is IMMUNE (it never touches the residual). So superposition may be exactly the regime where broad-cell-editing beats linear concept-removal.\n\n## PRODUCE (write to experiments/fra_hierarchy/THEORY_HIERARCHY.md):\n1. **THEORY of broad×broad cell-cutting**: what does cutting a (broad × broad) cell DO mechanistically vs the specific×specific (bigram) case? Formalize the breadth axis (feature fires on many tokens) and height axis (abstraction/hierarchy as OR-of-children). The exact statement of WHEN it works (the concept→concept link must be carried by an attention edge: broad-query-feature × broad-key-feature) vs fails (direction/OV-routed). The superposition connection, made precise (the interference collateral of a linear concept-removal vs the immunity of a score-space cell-edit).\n2. **THEORY of the regression protocol**: the optimization formulation (regress behavior delta onto per-cell ablation effects; sparse/L1 for minimal cell-set; collateral-constrained). How it generalizes top-K and differential cells. What it buys (finds non-obvious / abstract / multi-cell edits).\n3. **A CONCRETE, BUILDABLE SYNTHETIC-MODEL SPEC (the deliverable we build FIRST)** demonstrating BOTH: (i) a broad×broad attention cell is cuttable SELECTIVELY, and (ii) the regression protocol RECOVERS the planted broad×broad cell from a target, validated against ground truth. Specify: the data-generating process (hierarchical/superposed features: broad = OR of N narrow children; a PERSONA broad feature and several DOMAIN broad features); the attention head/task (a small/hand-built head that ROUTES the broad PERSONA-query feature to a broad DOMAIN-key feature — the 'generalization' mechanism, e.g. persona-active → attend-to/amplify domain content); the planted association to cut (persona × domain_X); the SELECTIVITY metrics (cut persona×domain_X: domain_X-misalignment removed; persona×domain_Y preserved; domain_X aligned-processing preserved); the SUPERPOSITION SWEEP (vary overlap ρ → linear-steer collateral grows, cell-edit stays ~0 → A(ρ) curve); the REGRESSION validation (does the fitted sparse cell-mask recover the planted (persona,domain_X) cell?). Prefer a HAND-BUILT toy attention head (analytically transparent, you set W_Q,W_K,ω and the features) as the first build, with a trained-head variant as a follow-up. State EXACTLY what plot/number proves each claim. Keep it small and runnable on a single GPU / even CPU.\n4. The decisive hand-off to the real-LLM evaluator: what to look for to tell whether a real concept→concept behavior (EM flagship; what else — refusal-persona×topic, sycophancy×context, format-persona×domain?) is attention-routed and thus broad-cell-cuttable.\n\nBe concrete and rigorous; the synthetic spec is the priority and must be immediately buildable. Return a tight summary + confirm THEORY_HIERARCHY.md is written."},"uuid":"dd75fd1d-8fdb-41ad-a75c-e0b4d1f477b5","timestamp":"2026-06-11T22:52:37.279Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
