{"parentUuid":"1dcc3fe5-c5be-40a0-93dd-116bebb73b60","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6f22e38681eea6df","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01W8MxKGRAsA8rHhUbWSpSyb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MmsADzgE4byRAg1M61asEC","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win/THEORY.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6965,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11763,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11763,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CbxHxVb4LBTFJNfDrk8VW","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"ffcf2152-82a5-42b2-a325-dd52188b5fc8","timestamp":"2026-06-11T22:52:41.862Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"ffcf2152-82a5-42b2-a325-dd52188b5fc8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b32a9976-0e68-4179-85b4-24af33ceaeb4","agentId":"a6f22e38681eea6df","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MmsADzgE4byRAg1M61asEC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# FRA Theory (Fable, sprint-2 — converged @ cycle 3)\n2\t\n3\t## Mechanistic theory\n4\tWHAT FRA UNIQUELY COMPUTES. A head h's pre-softmax score is a bilinear form on the post-norm residual: S^h[q,k] = (x_q W_Q^h)·(x_k W_K^h)/√d_h (row-vector convention; biases contribute pure row/column/constant terms). Substituting the SAE decomposition x_t = Σ_μ u^μ_t f_μ + e_t yields the EXACT partition S^h[q,k] = Σ_{μν} u^μ_q·u^ν_k·ω^h_{μν} + (feature×error) + (error×error) + bias terms, with ω^h_{μν} = (f_μ W_Q^h)·(f_ν W_K^h)/√d_h the weight-space pair coupling. Each (μ,ν) CELL is a multiplicative AND: its value u^μ_q·u^ν_k is identically zero unless the query-content feature AND the key-content feature both fire (u ≥ 0 under ReLU/JumpReLU). This is the only exact additive decomposition in the attention pathway that lives in the JOINT (query-content × key-content) function space: the OV side (C^OV = A·u^λ·⟨f_λ W_OV, d⟩) is merely linear-given-pattern, and the post-softmax pattern admits no canonical decomposition (the denominator couples all cells across all keys; attribution requires the Jacobian ∂A_qk/∂s_qj = A_qk(1_{k=j}−A_qj) and the centered OV profile g̃^h_{q,j} = A^h_{qj}(g^h_j−ḡ^h_q) — but the EDIT needs no linearization because it acts on s BEFORE the softmax). THE EDIT AND ITS EXPRESSIVE UNIQUENESS. The FRA edit subtracts c·u^μ_q·u^ν_k·ω^h_{μν} from one head's scores wherever the conjunction fires. With the SAE gates frozen it is exactly a support-gated rank-1 update of the head's bilinear form, ΔW^h_QK ∝ −c·ω_{μν}·e_μᵀe_ν restricted to {(q,k): u^μ_q>0 ∧ u^ν_k>0}; its only causal channel is that head's softmax→OV transport. FRA additionally supports SET ALGEBRA over cells: UNIONS across pairs/heads — including whole feature FAMILIES (class-level edits: cut every (attribute-query × value-class-key) cell at once) — and DIFFERENCES (differential cells = target-edge top-M minus sibling-edge top-M), which buy back target-specificity when siblings share an endpoint (measured: sibling separability 1.9×→7.9× at a quantified reach cost 58%→33%). A linear residual steer Δ (ActAdd/DoM/CAA/projection-removal), even gated by an ARBITRARY content gate g(x), is doubly weaker. (a) SCORE-SPACE EXPRESSIVITY: a gated query-side write changes scores by δs[q,k] = g(x_q)·(Δ W_Q^h)·(x_k W_K^h)ᵀ/√d, which varies over keys only through x_k's projection onto ONE fixed pullback direction v = Δ W_Q^h W_K^hᵀ. Cancelling a single cell requires ⟨x_k, v⟩ ∝ u^ν(x_k) for ALL k — impossible: u^ν is a thresholded nonlinearity of x_k, and even its linear part forces hitting the entire ν-ROW of the bilinear form plus every key cosine-close to v. A steer can imitate a row or a column of W_QK, never a cell — and a fortiori never a cell-difference or a family-union. (b) RESIDUAL BROADCAST: the write Δ is deposited into the stream and read by EVERY consumer at the gated positions — all heads' Q, K AND V, the MLP, every later layer. Gating restricts WHERE the steer fires, never WHAT reads it. These two facts ARE the measured separability gap: at matched on-target removal, a content-gated projection-removal steer strong enough to suppress the behavior destroys the content everywhere it legitimately appears (legit-content KL 1.77–2.64 nats), while the FRA cell-edit leaves it at ~0.000–0.0016 (≈1,000–26,000×), because legitimate occurrences fail the conjunction. THE MAGNITUDE LAW (validated at both extremes): A ≈ reuse(marginal endpoint)/reuse(conjunction), with reuse measured ON THE EVAL/DEPLOYMENT SUPPORT (naive corpus firing rates are degenerate — the s5 failure). A ~ 10³–10⁴ when the conjunction is unique (retrieval 1100×, acronym 26,000×); A → ~1.9× floor when a GENERIC endpoint makes the conjunction recur (shared-endpoint sibling test). SHARPENED COROLLARY (cycle 2): the discriminating endpoint — usually the query — must be distinctive CONTENT (a specific token/feature), NOT a generic ROLE feature. Positionally-resolved retrieval (box/entity identity) uses a generic \"queried-slot\" feature, so the (query × value) conjunction recurs across siblings and FRA cannot separate them (box A=7.9× partial only at weak base; entity-PII no-op at strong base). Every confirmed win has a content query: induction (query = token X), copy-suppression (query = about-to-predict-X), acronym (query = the spelled letters), in-context backdoor (query = the trigger content). NONLINEARITY LEDGER (what is exact where): RMSNorm is a frozen per-position SCALAR × diag(γ) — it commutes into the activations given the cached rms, so the score decomposition is exact on Gemma (edge-magnitude ratio 1.07 confirms). GPT-2 LayerNorm adds the fixed centering projector (I−11ᵀ/d); the 50–75% edge-reconstruction shortfall is a LN-folding-convention artifact, not an FRA property; ln1.hook_normalized is the gold-standard hookpoint but no public SAE suite ships it, and the grms check showed the hookpoint is not the limiter on RMSNorm models. RoPE is a per-position ROTATION applied AFTER projection: ω^h_{μν}(q−k) = ((f_μ W_Q^h)R_q)·((f_ν W_K^h)R_k)ᵀ/√d depends only on the relative offset (block structure R_qR_kᵀ = R_{q−k}) — still exact per edge; the edit stays content-addressed with an offset-dependent coefficient. GPT-2's learned absolute positional embeddings enter simply as residual content (positional features → the CCF sink-mask handles them). Gemma's soft-cap s ↦ 50·tanh(s/50) is the ONE true nonlinearity between the bilinear sum and the softmax: cells are exact pre-cap, and an edit Δs reaches the pattern attenuated by tanh′(s/50) ≤ 1, so edits are compressed exactly on saturated edges. This — plus the SAE-unexplained score fraction (the error×· terms) and granularity×top-K matching (65k GemmaScope is the sweet spot; 1M-width fragments an edge across too many tiny cells for a fixed pair budget) — is the complete account of FRA's suppression-reach ceiling. The ceiling bounds REACH, never separability: whatever FRA removes, it removes only on the conjunction's support. SUMMARY: FRA computes the exact joint query-content×key-content functional decomposition of attention selection, and hands you the corresponding cell-level (and cell-set-level) weight edit whose causal support is a content conjunction — the missing middle between direction steers (marginal + broadcast to all readers) and position patches (specific but not content-addressed).\n5\t\n6\t## Win checklist\n7\t1. EDGE-ROUTED (CCF-high): the behavior's proximate cause is pre-softmax score mass on identifiable attention edges, dominated by non-sink content×content feature pairs after sink-masking (CCF reliable on gpt2-small; on gemma the current sink-mask over-kills late layers, so certify behaviorally via LBNR). Kills positional/BOS edges (CCF=0.000) and output-direction behaviors with no score-space cause (weight-baked sleeper).\n8\t2. LOAD-BEARING & NON-REDUNDANT (LBNR-R ≈ 1, measured BEHAVIORALLY with CAUSAL head-finding): cutting the identified feature-pair edge across ALL heads that carry it (heads ranked by causal edge-cut effect, never raw attention — raw attention selects positional/sink heads) removes the downstream behavior, and no backup circuit OR alternative cue restores it. Kills IOI (R=−0.39, backups overcompensate), docstring (R=0.08), delimiter matching (R=0.23, grammar provides redundant cues), gemma knowledge-conflict (R=0.24).\n9\t3. DIRECT CONSUMPTION: the behavior IS the edge's OV-transported content (the attended token's write into the output), not a downstream MLP computation that merely reads the attended information — so LBNR must be evaluated on the behavioral metric, never on attention or an intermediate. Kills greater-than (the > is MLP-computed; edge-cut dents behavior only 0.98→0.87).\n10\t4. CONJUNCTION-SPECIFIC ON THE EVAL DISTRIBUTION, with a DISTINCTIVE-CONTENT discriminating endpoint: at least one endpoint feature legitimately recurs in deployment (so every direction/content-gated steer pays collateral), while the specific conjunction does NOT recur legitimately — which requires the discriminating endpoint (usually the query) to be distinctive CONTENT (a specific token/phrase/letter-state feature), not a generic ROLE feature; positionally-resolved identity (box/entity slots) fails this clause by construction. If siblings share the value endpoint, differential cells (target-edge minus sibling-edge) must retain enough non-shared score mass; if the goal is class-level removal, the UNION of the family's cells must be enumerable. Kills rare-dedicated-token triggers (a direction is already surgical, A→1) and generic-role-query retrieval (sibling A=1.9×; entity-PII no-op).\n11\t5. REACH (bounds removal completeness, not the win/lose verdict): SAE-explained fraction of the edge score × causal head coverage × top-K pair budget — with SAE granularity matched to K (65k GemmaScope sweet spot; 1M fragments at fixed K) — × soft-cap headroom tanh′(s/50) must clear the softmax margin on every carrying head at faithful scale c≈1–2, so that a matched-removal operating point EXISTS at which the separability comparison is defined.\n12\t\n13\t**Underlying reason:** The whole checklist is one separability statement. The behavior's minimal sufficient cause must be a SEPARABLE PRODUCT TERM u^μ_q·u^ν_k inside one (or an enumerable few) heads' score functions, whose support is disjoint from legitimate use of its endpoints ON THE EVAL DISTRIBUTION. When it is: (i) the FRA edit's support is exactly the conjunction's support and its only causal channel is those heads' softmaxes, so its collateral scales with reuse(conjunction|eval) — ~0 when the pairing is the targeted/malicious thing; (ii) ANY linear residual steer, however gated, must either suppress a marginal endpoint — its score effect is confined to a row/column of the bilinear form (one fixed pullback direction over keys) — or write into the residual stream where all heads' Q/K/V, the MLP, and every later layer read it; so its collateral scales with reuse(marginal|eval) × (number of residual readers). The win ratio at matched removal is therefore A ≈ reuse(marginal|eval)/reuse(conjunction|eval), validated at both extremes: ~10³–10⁴ when the conjunction is unique (retrieval 1100×, acronym 26,000×) and a ~1.9× floor when a generic role endpoint makes the conjunction recur (shared-endpoint sibling), with differential cells buying specificity back (7.9×) at a quantified reach cost (58%→33%). CCF certifies the cause lives in score space; LBNR certifies the conjunction is the unique carrier (against both backup circuits and redundant distributional cues); direct-consumption certifies the product term's output IS the behavior; conjunction-specificity-with-content-discriminator certifies the ratio's denominator is small and its numerator large; reach certifies the basis can express enough of the term to act on. Each failure mode is the negation of exactly one factor.\n14\t\n15\t**Failure modes:**\n16\t- OUTPUT-DIRECTION ROUTING (weight-baked sleeper, emergent misalignment): the payload is written through OV/unembedding as a residual DIRECTION with near-zero legitimate reuse; there is no score-space cause to edit, and DoM/SVD on the marginal direction is already surgical — no bilinear gap exists (negates edge-routing and the reuse gap).\n17\t- REDUNDANT / SELF-REPAIRING CIRCUITS (IOI name-movers R=−0.39 with backup attention 0.34→0.69; docstring R=0.08): cutting the edge triggers backup heads that restore — or overshoot — the behavior; the conjunction is not the unique carrier, so the edit is precise but behaviorally inert (negates LBNR).\n18\t- DISTRIBUTIONAL REDUNDANCY OF STRUCTURAL PREDICTION (delimiter/quote-type matching, CCF=0.732 but R=+0.23 — the cycle-2 negative class): the edge is a genuine content×content conjunction, but the predicted output is ALSO derivable from many other cues the distribution provides (grammar gives many ways to know a paren must close), so the edge is not load-bearing even with no dedicated backup circuit (negates LBNR by cue-redundancy rather than head-redundancy).\n19\t- DISTRIBUTED / DIRECTION-ROUTED IN-CONTEXT BEHAVIOR (many-shot jailbreak; binding R=−0.89; gemma knowledge-conflict R=0.24): the behavior rides a distributed ICL task-direction across many weak edges, not a separable pair; worse, the injected behavior can be representationally identical to a legitimate one ('jailbroken enthusiasm' = 'genuine enthusiasm'), so NO method removes it cleanly — there is no separable link to cut (negates edge-routing and LBNR).\n20\t- DOWNSTREAM NONLINEAR CONSUMPTION (greater-than): the QK edge is real and content-conjunctive, but an MLP computes the behavior from the attended information; cutting the edge controls the attending, not the computation (negates direct consumption).\n21\t- CONJUNCTION RECURRENCE — generic role endpoint, positional identity, or collision (shared-endpoint sibling A=1.9×; entity-PII differential no-op at strong base; acronym 'Unit' duplicate): the target conjunction's support overlaps legitimate instances of the SAME pair, either literally (duplicate target word) or because the discriminating endpoint is a generic role feature ('box-query', 'entity-slot') so identity is resolved POSITIONALLY, not by content — FRA's content-addressing correctly fires on the siblings too; collateral by design, A collapses toward 1. Partial rescue: differential cells (1.9→7.9×) at reach cost, IF non-shared mass exists (negates conjunction-specificity).\n22\t- REACH CEILING (Gemma backdoor removal 1/4→3/4 at 16k→65k; 1M-width regression at fixed K; GPT-2 LN-centering 50–75% reconstruction; soft-cap compression tanh′(s/50) on saturated edges; uncovered carrying heads): the SAE basis is too coarse, too fine for the pair budget, the folding drops centering, the cap eats the edit, or a carrying head is missed — FRA cannot hit the matched-removal operating point, so the win is capped or undefined even though separability holds for what it can remove (negates reach).\n23\t- POSITIONAL / SINK EDGE (BOS: raw attention 0.98 but CCF=0.000; lost-in-the-middle): the edge is selected by position, not content; a position-patch is the correct tool and content-addressing adds nothing (negates the content clause of edge-routing)."}]},"uuid":"93b21f9d-1605-4af9-9a27-d03208614255","timestamp":"2026-06-11T22:52:41.878Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ffcf2152-82a5-42b2-a325-dd52188b5fc8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"93b21f9d-1605-4af9-9a27-d03208614255","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6f22e38681eea6df","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01W8MxKGRAsA8rHhUbWSpSyb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C5qttHPJWnJnS5RKQscHi3","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win/RESULTS_SUMMARY.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6965,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11763,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11763,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CbxHxVb4LBTFJNfDrk8VW","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"71408c0d-4549-4b5e-8b24-175ff37d9546","timestamp":"2026-06-11T22:52:42.337Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"71408c0d-4549-4b5e-8b24-175ff37d9546","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b32a9976-0e68-4179-85b4-24af33ceaeb4","agentId":"a6f22e38681eea6df","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C5qttHPJWnJnS5RKQscHi3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Feature-Resolved Attention: when, why, and how much it beats linear steering — results summary\n2\t\n3\t*Compressed per the writing guidelines: the narrative, the claims, the evidence. Source material:\n4\t`THEORY.md`, `CAMPAIGN_REPORT.md`, `summary.md`; figures `fig1_final.png`, `fig6_retrieval.png`,\n5\t`fig9_lbnr_tier2.png`, `fig_sprint2_summary.png`, `fig_magnitude_law.png`.*\n6\t\n7\t## The one-paragraph narrative\n8\t\n9\tFeature-Resolved Attention (FRA) decomposes a head's pre-softmax attention score, in an SAE basis, into\n10\tan exact sum of **cells** `S[q,k] = Σ_{μν} u^μ_q u^ν_k ω_{μν}`, each a multiplicative AND of a\n11\tquery-content feature and a key-content feature. The corresponding **cell-level weight edit** (a\n12\tsupport-gated rank-1 update of W_QK) is a capability **no linear residual steer can express**: a steer\n13\tcan imitate a *row or column* of the bilinear form but never a *cell*, and it broadcasts into the\n14\tresidual stream where every consumer reads it. We turn this into a *predictive* and *quantitative*\n15\taccount of when FRA earns its keep as a behavioral-intervention tool, validate it across five model\n16\tbehaviors, and map the boundary of its (narrow) win-class.\n17\t\n18\t## The claims\n19\t\n20\t**Claim 1 (the win, measured against the strongest fair baseline).** For behaviors carried by a\n21\tcontent-query × content-key attention edge, an FRA cell-edit suppresses the behavior while leaving the\n22\tendpoints' *other* uses essentially untouched, at **10³–10⁴× lower collateral** than the strongest fair\n23\t*linear* baseline — a content-gated projection-removal steer — at matched on-target removal.\n24\t*Evidence:* legit-content KL at matched removal: retrieval (gemma-2-2b) **0.0016 vs 1.77 nats (~1100×)**;\n25\tacronym letter-movers (gpt2) **~0 vs 2.64 (~26,000×)**; copy-suppression on natural text **0.000 vs ~2.0,\n26\tA=516×**. Head-ablation and output-direction suppression (the baselines reported pre-red-team) are\n27\t*strawmen* — they break the behavior everywhere; the position-patch is fair but position-tied (fails\n28\tcontent-addressed transfer). The decisive, fair comparison is the linear steer, and FRA wins it by orders\n29\tof magnitude.\n30\t\n31\t**Claim 2 (the magnitude law).** The advantage obeys **A ≈ reuse(marginal endpoint) / reuse(conjunction)**,\n32\treuse measured on the evaluation distribution. *Evidence:* validated as a **quantitative curve** — in a\n33\tcontrolled sweep of N siblings sharing a value, generic pairs (conjunction recurs) give A flat at ~1\n34\t(1.4→2.0), while differential cells (conjunction made unique) give A growing ≈ N (6.3→13.4→23.8 over\n35\tN=2..4). This is the correct form of the magnitude predictor an earlier corpus-firing-rate attempt failed\n36\tto capture.\n37\t\n38\t**Claim 3 (the boundary — a predictive checklist, and a narrow win-class).** FRA gives a clean win iff:\n39\t(1) edge-routed (CCF-high, not positional/output-direction), (2) load-bearing & non-redundant (causal\n40\tedge-cut R≈1, no backups/alternative cues), (3) direct consumption (the behavior *is* the OV-transported\n41\tcontent, not downstream MLP), (4) conjunction-specific with a **distinctive-content discriminating query**\n42\t(a specific token/feature, not a generic role), (5) reach (SAE-explained × head-coverage × top-K clears\n43\tthe softmax margin). *Evidence:* confirmed wins — induction (15×), in-context backdoor (25×),\n44\tcopy-suppression (516×), retrieval (1100×), acronym (26,000×). Theory-predicted failures, each isolating\n45\tone clause — weight-baked sleeper (output direction, c1), greater-than (MLP-downstream, c3), IOI (backups,\n46\tc2), docstring/delimiter (redundant, c2), many-shot jailbreak (direction-routed), PII/entity retrieval\n47\t(positional/role query, c4), class-union (token-specific keys, c4). **Most established-benchmark behaviors\n48\tfall outside the win-class** — this is the central, honest finding: FRA is a *specialized* instrument, the\n49\t\"missing middle\" between direction steers (marginal + broadcast) and position patches (specific but not\n50\tcontent-addressed).\n51\t\n52\t## So what (why it matters)\n53\t\n54\t(i) A *principled, predictive* criterion for a bilinear interpretability primitive — you can decide\n55\tbefore you intervene. (ii) A demonstration that the bilinear (QK) structure of attention is **load-bearing**:\n56\tthere exist interventions a content-addressed *linear* steer provably cannot match. (iii) An honest map of\n57\twhere this helps — narrow, but real, and relevant to memorization/copy control, retrieval steering, and\n58\tin-context backdoor removal.\n59\t\n60\t## Methodological contributions (reusable)\n61\t- The **corrected Tier-2 metric**: legit-content KL vs a content-gated *projection-removal* linear steer\n62\t  at matched on-target removal (not A-ratio vs head-ablation strawmen). Sprint-1's red-team produced this.\n63\t- **Causal head-finding** (rank heads by edge-cut effect, not raw attention, which selects positional heads).\n64\t- **Differential cells** (target-edge minus sibling-edge) to recover target-specificity when siblings\n65\t  share an endpoint, at a quantified reach cost.\n66\t\n67\t## Relation to the prior result (→ appendix)\n68\tThe earlier write-up established the *first* FRA behavioral win — association-specific control of an\n69\tinduction edge, ~15× lower collateral than the fairest linear steer — and the sleeper-agent *bridge*\n70\t(weight-baked backdoor → DoM/SVD wins; in-context backdoor → FRA-QK wins), unifying removal-method choice\n71\tunder \"suppress what uniquely carries the behavior.\" This work subsumes that as one entry in the win-class,\n72\tadds the exact cell/set-algebra theory, the magnitude law, the corrected fair metric, and the boundary map.\n73\t"}]},"uuid":"9d0fcc18-0dcb-4871-a4c3-0f62454ba3c6","timestamp":"2026-06-11T22:52:42.342Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"71408c0d-4549-4b5e-8b24-175ff37d9546","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"9d0fcc18-0dcb-4871-a4c3-0f62454ba3c6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6f22e38681eea6df","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01W8MxKGRAsA8rHhUbWSpSyb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KUDMQ2p3kpEbGmeA5TwcCa","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_hierarchy/CAMPAIGN.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6965,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11763,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":306,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11763},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6965,"output_tokens":306,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11763,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11763,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CbxHxVb4LBTFJNfDrk8VW","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"f2b455dd-3a4a-49d2-9d25-8950ea0420b6","timestamp":"2026-06-11T22:52:43.038Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"f2b455dd-3a4a-49d2-9d25-8950ea0420b6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"b32a9976-0e68-4179-85b4-24af33ceaeb4","agentId":"a6f22e38681eea6df","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KUDMQ2p3kpEbGmeA5TwcCa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# FRA HIERARCHY campaign — broad×broad cell-cutting (started 2026-06-11)\n2\t\n3\tHYPOTHESIS (PI): confirmed FRA wins are all specific-feature->single-token (lowest hierarchy rung; cutting a cell = cutting a bigram). The INTERESTING regime = BROAD features (many words) + HIGH hierarchy (abstract concepts). Flagship: cut (misaligned-PERSONA feature x DOMAIN feature) -> SELECTIVELY block EM generalizing to that domain, preserving persona elsewhere + domain's aligned processing (a linear persona-direction removal can't: all-or-nothing).\n4\tKEY RISK: FRA only cuts ATTENTION-routed links. Concept->concept via OV/MLP/direction (em_svd showed EM is a DIRECTION) is invisible to FRA. (1) CAN a broad×broad ATTENTION cell be cut selectively? [SYNTHETIC, PRIORITY]. (2) WHICH real concept-links are attention-routed? [real-LLM hunt].\n5\tTEAM (targeted): 1 theory (Fable), 1 real-LLM-behaviour brainstorm, 1 real-world evaluator, 1 red-team. SYNTHETIC-FIRST.\n6\tSame rules: RunPod RP_API_KEY_MATS, budget-conscious, no local compute, parse-gate jobs, new job id per run.\n7\tRefs: THEORY.md (converged FRA theory), SynthSAEBench arxiv 2602.14687 (synthetic ground-truth features w/ hierarchy+superposition), Toy Models of Superposition.\n8\t\n9\t## STATE\n10\t- PHASE 1/theory: theory agent designing broad×broad theory + buildable synthetic spec. POD relaunching.\n11\t"}]},"uuid":"d742daee-2557-4a2c-b51d-428f7afc83a0","timestamp":"2026-06-11T22:52:43.044Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f2b455dd-3a4a-49d2-9d25-8950ea0420b6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.