{"parentUuid":"be32f4d7-3fc3-4855-86f3-a87c3429648e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a6f22e38681eea6df","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01Ln74TWSa1xnwA1pu3hEPPG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011VKDboziN34pjoCpHdADQy","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_hierarchy/CAMPAIGN.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":459,"cache_read_input_tokens":108907,"output_tokens":102,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":459},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":102,"cache_read_input_tokens":108907,"cache_creation_input_tokens":459,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":459,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CbxK2ZJmpRLz95yzT2oQU","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"1a93807d-3f26-4f82-8af2-2254e8e119fc","timestamp":"2026-06-11T23:06:44.745Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
{"parentUuid":"1a93807d-3f26-4f82-8af2-2254e8e119fc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"69a29073-a7e9-4d4b-9e4e-c89ce2bd472b","agentId":"a6f22e38681eea6df","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011VKDboziN34pjoCpHdADQy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# FRA HIERARCHY campaign — broad×broad cell-cutting (started 2026-06-11)\n2\t\n3\tHYPOTHESIS (PI): confirmed FRA wins are all specific-feature->single-token (lowest hierarchy rung; cutting a cell = cutting a bigram). The INTERESTING regime = BROAD features (many words) + HIGH hierarchy (abstract concepts). Flagship: cut (misaligned-PERSONA feature x DOMAIN feature) -> SELECTIVELY block EM generalizing to that domain, preserving persona elsewhere + domain's aligned processing (a linear persona-direction removal can't: all-or-nothing).\n4\tKEY RISK: FRA only cuts ATTENTION-routed links. Concept->concept via OV/MLP/direction (em_svd showed EM is a DIRECTION) is invisible to FRA. (1) CAN a broad×broad ATTENTION cell be cut selectively? [SYNTHETIC, PRIORITY]. (2) WHICH real concept-links are attention-routed? [real-LLM hunt].\n5\tTEAM (targeted): 1 theory (Fable), 1 real-LLM-behaviour brainstorm, 1 real-world evaluator, 1 red-team. SYNTHETIC-FIRST.\n6\tSame rules: RunPod RP_API_KEY_MATS, budget-conscious, no local compute, parse-gate jobs, new job id per run.\n7\tRefs: THEORY.md (converged FRA theory), SynthSAEBench arxiv 2602.14687 (synthetic ground-truth features w/ hierarchy+superposition), Toy Models of Superposition.\n8\t\n9\t## STATE\n10\t- PHASE 1/theory: theory agent designing broad×broad theory + buildable synthetic spec. POD relaunching.\n11\t\n12\t## SECOND THREAD (PI add): the REGRESSION protocol — FIT which cells to cut\n13\tInstead of top-magnitude cell selection (only works for single-token specifics) or hand-crafted differential cells: given a TARGET (behavior/logit delta, attention-pattern change, collateral budget), SOLVE for the cell-mask (sparse/L1 regression of behavior-change onto per-cell ablations; \"smallest cell-set that removes the behavior under a collateral cap\"). Subsumes top-K + differential cells; the natural way to FIND broad concept-cells. SYNTHETIC validates it (does the fitted mask recover the PLANTED broad×broad cell?). The two threads are ONE program: regression = protocol, broad×broad = regime, synthetic = ground-truth testbed.\n14\t\n15\t## PLAN (synthetic-first, then team)\n16\t1. Theory agent (Fable, RUNNING a6f22e38681eea6df) -> THEORY_HIERARCHY.md: broad×broad theory + regression theory + buildable synthetic spec.\n17\t2. I BUILD + RUN the synthetic model (PRIORITY): (i) broad×broad attention cell cuttable selectively; (ii) regression recovers the planted cell; (iii) superposition sweep A(rho); vs linear persona-steer (all-or-nothing + interference). On pod ivccjcfk9najzb.\n18\t3. IF synthetic validates -> spin up the rest of the TEAM (real-LLM-behaviour brainstorm [EM flagship], real-world evaluator, red-team) + autonomous loop to test on real LLMs.\n19\t4. IF synthetic fails (broad×broad NOT cuttable / regression doesn't recover) -> report honestly, that bounds the direction.\n20\t\n21\t## STATE\n22\t- PHASE 1/theory: a6f22e38681eea6df running (synthetic spec). POD ivccjcfk9najzb booting. NEXT: build synthetic from spec.\n23\t\n24\t## THIRD PILLAR (PI): MEASURE attention-routedness + FRA IMPROVES CIRCUIT TRACING\n25\t(A) MEASURE the extent a concept->concept link is attention-routed vs OV/MLP/direction: probes (cheap, only show readable DIRECTION) < path-patching/EAP (headline dial = FRACTION of causal effect via attention edges vs MLP/direct) < circuit tracing/attribution graphs/transcoders (closest match). \n26\t(B) THESIS: FRA = the MISSING QK PIECE in circuit attribution. Circuit tracing localizes WHICH heads/edges + uses attention PATTERN but treats QK SCORE as black box; only intervention = head/edge ablation. FRA resolves the attention-routed edge into CELLS -> identifies WHICH content-conjunction carries the link + cuts ONLY it (more surgical than head ablation). PIPELINE: EAP localize+measure-routed-fraction -> FRA resolve edge into cells + cut broad×broad conjunction -> show FRA cut MORE selective (lower collateral) than head/edge ablation. = the paper-worthy contribution (FRA augments circuit tracing, not competes with steering).\n27\t(C) SYNTHETIC SPINE = a KNOWN TUNABLE ROUTING SPLIT alpha: fraction alpha of persona->domain generalization via ATTENTION cell, (1-alpha) via MLP/DIRECTION path. Validates: (1) EAP recovers true alpha; (2) on attention-routed part FRA cell-cut beats head-ablation; (3) alpha->0 FRA correctly cuts nothing (honest failure) while direction-removal still works -> WHEN each tool wins. (addendum sent to theory agent.)\n28\t"}]},"uuid":"a262c702-cda2-4a87-b423-fca0cffade22","timestamp":"2026-06-11T23:06:44.765Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1a93807d-3f26-4f82-8af2-2254e8e119fc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/dmitrymanning-coe/Documents/Research/FRA/fra_proj/experiments/fra_win","sessionId":"8a660228-bde0-4e60-bfe2-aafb33fe0b4d","version":"2.1.170","gitBranch":"autoresearch/fra-behavioral-win","slug":"moonlit-churning-gem"}
